  <content>
    <section class="learning-objectives" id="sect-00008">
      <title>Learning Objectives</title>
      <para id="para-00002">By the end of this section, you will be able to</para>
        <list id="list-00002" list-type="bulleted">
          <item>Describe the method and measures for how infant cognition is studied</item>
          <item>Describe the types of memory and what is known for memory development during this age range</item>
          <item>Explain the major cognitive-developmental theories relevant to early childhood</item>
        </list>
    </section>
    <para id="para-00001">Despite changes in the leading cause of deaths in the middle adulthood age demographic,
      <term class="no-emphasis" id="term-00001">cardiovascular disease</term> (CVD) is a steady and consistent number 2. While CVD is not random it can often be unexpected. There are a number of contributing factors related to cardiovascular health.</para>
      <para id="para-00005">WW-TEST notes that this module is testing some art issues (art against feature box shaded backgrounds, PNG art), tables, and lists.</para>
      <section id="sect-00009">
        <title>[H2]Metabolism and Endocrine</title>
        <para id="para-00006">
          The rate of <term class="no-emphasis" id="term-00002">obesity</term> increases in middle-age with the loss of muscle to fat and a slower <term class="no-emphasis" id="term-00003">metabolic rate</term>. Obesity is associated with increased risks of other conditions like hypertension and diabetes. It is also increased with slightly higher risk of cancer (American Cancer Society, 2023). Metabolic syndrome is a related condition in which obesity and insulin resistance can lead to heart disease, stroke, and diabetes.
        </para>
        <para id="para-00009">
          Diabetes is a chronic condition where the pancreas fails to produce enough insulin to break down sugar. <term id="term-00004">Type II diabetes</term> is typically a result of aging and often associated with weight and sedentariness. It has been an increasing problem with over 30,000 middle age adults dying from complications with diabetes in 2020 (CDC, 2020) and disproportionately impacts minority groups. The chronic nature of poorly regulated diabetes causes complications such as kidney failure, retinopathy, and neuropathy, particularly in the lower extremities.
        </para>
        <note class="it-depends" id="note-00001">
          <title>Feature Box with Art against HEX #FFF7E5 Background</title>
          <para id="para-00010">
            WW-test to assess art output against different feature box background colors. This should be the box with the yellow background. Art: please review output.
          </para>
          <figure id="Figure09_02_Stages1">
