        <para id="para-00017">
          Overall, maintaining general health is a critical aspect of maintaining brain health in middle adulthood. Most changes at this stage are minimal and do not show major differences and don’t vary significantly from brains at earlier ages. Components of secondary ageing show the greatest such as stress, chronic and acute diseases are likely the largest contributors to any deficits in brain functioning.
        </para>
      </section>
